<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>LLMs in Medicine - Infographic Poster</title>
<style>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    background: #F5F7FA;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
  #container {
    width: 1600px;
    min-height: 2263px;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="container"></div>
<script src="/app/vendor/infographic.min.js"></script>
<script>
const syntax = `infographic list-zigzag-down-compact-card
data
  title Large Language Models in Medicine
  desc Opportunities, Risks, and the Path Forward • Medical AI &amp; Digital Health Conference 2024
  lists
    - label The Rise of LLMs in Healthcare
      desc Foundation models trained on vast text corpora are rapidly entering clinical practice, biomedical research, and medical education. Over 500 peer-reviewed publications appeared in 2023 alone, and the global healthcare LLM market is projected to reach $10.5 billion by 2030.
      icon brain circuit
    - label Benchmark Performance: GPT-4 Scores &gt;90% on USMLE
      value &gt;90%
      desc GPT-4 exceeded the ~60% passing threshold on all three steps of the US Medical Licensing Examination. Med-PaLM 2 scored 86.5% on MedQA. Earlier models like GPT-3.5 barely passed (~60%). These results demonstrate substantial medical knowledge encoding.
      icon award
    - label Safety Concern: Hallucination Rate Up to 30%
      value Up to 30%
      desc LLMs fabricate plausible but incorrect medical information — including fake citations and clinical recommendations — in up to 30% of medical question-answering outputs. Benchmark performance does not guarantee clinical safety or reliability.
      icon alert triangle
    - label Key Clinical and Research Applications
      desc Clinical Documentation: automated notes, discharge summaries (pilot deployments). Diagnostic Support: differential diagnosis, radiology interpretation (research stage). Patient Communication: answering questions, simplifying jargon (early adoption). Medical Education: exam prep, case-based learning (active use). Biomedical Research: literature synthesis, hypothesis generation (emerging).
      icon stethoscope
    - label Risks, Limitations, and Ethical Concerns
      desc Hallucinations generate false medical information including fabricated citations. Training data bias may amplify care disparities across demographic groups. Patient data in prompts raises HIPAA and GDPR compliance risks. Most evaluations use MCQ benchmarks, not prospective clinical trials. Clinician automation bias risks over-reliance on unverified AI outputs.
      icon shield warning
    - label A Framework for Responsible Deployment
      desc 1. Rigorous prospective evaluation in diverse clinical settings. 2. Human-in-the-loop design ensuring clinician oversight of all LLM-generated outputs. 3. Transparent reporting of model limitations, training data, and failure modes. 4. Equity audits to assess differential performance across patient populations. 5. Regulatory alignment with FDA, EMA, and WHO guidance on AI-based medical devices.
      icon clipboard check
theme
  palette #0B1D3A #38858A #6D8BAA #F5F7FA #E8734A
  base
    text
      font-family Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif`;

const infographic = new AntVInfographic.Infographic({
  container: '#container',
  width: 1600,
  height: 2263,
});

infographic.render(syntax).then(() => {
  console.log('Infographic rendered successfully');
  window.__infographicReady = true;
}).catch(err => {
  console.error('Render error:', err);
});

document.fonts?.ready.then(() => {
  infographic.render(syntax).then(() => {
    console.log('Infographic re-rendered after fonts loaded');
    window.__infographicReady = true;
  });
}).catch(() => {});
</script>
</body>
</html>
